 "name": "Alcohol Exposure in an Urban Square – Scene Ratings",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Pastor et al. (2022), Int. J. Environ. Res. Public Health 19(15): 9192. Respondents see three 3D-rendered scenes (Lumion/SketchUp) of Lavapiés Square, Madrid, with null, medium (11 alcohol elements) and high (23 alcohol elements: advertising, litter, people drinking) alcohol exposure, shown side by side as in the original Google Form. For every scene they rate presence of alcohol-related elements (1–10), resemblance to the real square (1–3), comfort (1–10), acceptance (1–10) and acceptance with children present (1–10), then answer the original sociodemographic questions. The scenes are the paper's Figures 3, 5 and 6 (CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is removed if the authors object. Original result (159 adults, Madrid region): median comfort 9 / 7 / 6 and acceptance with children 10 / 7 / 5 from null to high exposure (Kruskal–Wallis). Differences from the original study: (1) the scenes come from the paper's figures (about 730 px wide) rather than the original render files; (2) the free-text questions on neighbourhood (B4) and city of residence (B5) are left out; (3) the consent item adds an 18+ confirmation; (4) the original Spanish questionnaire is given in the authors' English translation.",
